			<h1>Qwant Search Engine</h1>
			<p class="intro">European privacy-first search with GDPR compliance and no tracking.</p>

			<nav class="toc">
				<h2>Contents</h2>
				<ol>
					<li><a href="#what-is">What is Qwant?</a></li>
					<li><a href="#features">Key Features</a></li>
					<li><a href="#privacy">Privacy & GDPR</a></li>
					<li><a href="#qwant-junior">Qwant Junior for Kids</a></li>
					<li><a href="#search-quality">Search Quality</a></li>
					<li><a href="#pros-cons">Pros and Cons</a></li>
					<li><a href="#setup">How to Use Qwant</a></li>
					<li><a href="#faq">FAQ</a></li>
				</ol>
			</nav>

			<section id="what-is">
				<h2>What is Qwant?</h2>
				<p>Qwant is a privacy-focused search engine headquartered in Paris, France. Founded in 2013, it's one of the few European search engines that aims to compete with Google while respecting user privacy.</p>

				<div class="highlight-box">
					<h3>Quick Facts</h3>
					<ul>
						<li><strong>Founded:</strong> 2013 (France)</li>
						<li><strong>Index:</strong> Own index + Bing</li>
						<li><strong>AI Features:</strong> Optional only</li>
						<li><strong>Tracking:</strong> None</li>
						<li><strong>Special:</strong> Kid-safe version (Qwant Junior)</li>
					</ul>
				</div>

				<p>Unlike Google, Qwant doesn't create user profiles, track your searches, or personalize results based on your history. Every search is neutral and private.</p>
			</section>

			<section id="features">
				<h2>Key Features</h2>

				<div class="feature-grid">
					<div class="feature-card">
						<h3>No Tracking</h3>
						<p>No cookies, no user profiles, no search history stored.</p>
					</div>
					<div class="feature-card">
						<h3>GDPR Compliant</h3>
						<p>Based in France, fully compliant with EU privacy laws.</p>
					</div>
					<div class="feature-card">
						<h3>Qwant Junior</h3>
						<p>Safe search for children with filtered content.</p>
					</div>
					<div class="feature-card">
						<h3>Qwant Maps</h3>
						<p>Privacy-respecting maps based on OpenStreetMap.</p>
					</div>
					<div class="feature-card">
						<h3>No Filter Bubbles</h3>
						<p>Everyone sees the same results - no personalization.</p>
					</div>
					<div class="feature-card">
						<h3>Own Index</h3>
						<p>Uses its own crawler supplemented by Bing.</p>
					</div>
				</div>

				<h3>Search Categories</h3>
				<p>Qwant organizes results into categories:</p>
				<ul>
					<li><strong>Web</strong> - Standard search results</li>
					<li><strong>News</strong> - Recent news articles</li>
					<li><strong>Images</strong> - Image search</li>
					<li><strong>Videos</strong> - Video results</li>
					<li><strong>Shopping</strong> - Product searches (in some regions)</li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section id="privacy">
				<h2>Privacy & GDPR</h2>

				<div class="engine-card">
					<div class="engine-header">
						<div class="engine-info">
							<span class="engine-tag green">GDPR Compliant</span>
							<span class="engine-tag green">EU-Based</span>
						</div>
					</div>

					<h3>What Qwant Doesn't Collect</h3>
					<ul>
						<li>Search history linked to your identity</li>
						<li>IP addresses (anonymized immediately)</li>
						<li>User profiles or accounts for tracking</li>
						<li>Browsing behavior across sites</li>
						<li>Personal data for advertising</li>
					</ul>

					<h3>GDPR Advantages</h3>
					<p>Being based in France gives Qwant several privacy advantages:</p>
					<ul>
						<li><strong>GDPR enforcement</strong> - Subject to strict EU data protection</li>
						<li><strong>No US jurisdiction</strong> - Not subject to US data requests</li>
						<li><strong>Right to erasure</strong> - EU users can request data deletion</li>
						<li><strong>Data minimization</strong> - Required to collect only necessary data</li>
					</ul>

					<h3>Transparency</h3>
					<p>Qwant publishes transparency reports showing government data requests. Since they don't store personal data, they have little to hand over even if legally required.</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section id="qwant-junior">
				<h2>Qwant Junior for Kids</h2>

				<div class="method-box">
					<h3>Safe Search for Children</h3>
					<p>Qwant Junior is designed for children aged 6-12 and used in French schools. It provides:</p>
					<ul>
						<li><strong>Filtered content</strong> - Blocks violence, adult content, drugs, etc.</li>
						<li><strong>No tracking</strong> - Same privacy as regular Qwant</li>
						<li><strong>No ads</strong> - No advertising targeted at children</li>
						<li><strong>Educational focus</strong> - Results prioritized for learning</li>
						<li><strong>Simple interface</strong> - Easy for kids to use</li>
					</ul>

					<p>Visit: <code>junior.qwant.com</code></p>
				</div>

				<p>Qwant Junior is approved by the French Ministry of Education and is widely used in French schools as a safe alternative to Google for student research.</p>
			</section>

			<section id="search-quality">
				<h2>Search Quality</h2>

				<h3>How Qwant Gets Results</h3>
				<p>Qwant uses a hybrid approach:</p>
				<ul>
					<li><strong>Own index</strong> - Qwant crawls the web independently</li>
					<li><strong>Bing partnership</strong> - Supplements with Microsoft Bing results</li>
					<li><strong>No Google</strong> - Doesn't use Google's index</li>
				</ul>

				<h3>Result Quality</h3>
				<p>Compared to Google, Qwant's results are:</p>
				<ul>
					<li><strong>Good for general searches</strong> - Most queries work well</li>
					<li><strong>Excellent for European content</strong> - Strong coverage of EU sites</li>
					<li><strong>Weaker for US-specific content</strong> - Some gaps in American content</li>
					<li><strong>Improving over time</strong> - Qwant continues to grow its index</li>
				</ul>

				<h3>No Filter Bubbles</h3>
				<p>Because Qwant doesn't track you, everyone sees the same results. There's no "filter bubble" where you only see content that confirms your existing views.</p>
			</section>

			<section id="pros-cons">
				<h2>Pros and Cons</h2>

				<div class="pros-cons">
					<div class="pros">
						<h4>Pros</h4>
						<ul>
							<li>Strong privacy protection</li>
							<li>GDPR compliant (EU-based)</li>
							<li>Kid-safe version available</li>
							<li>No AI by default</li>
							<li>Privacy-focused maps</li>
							<li>No filter bubbles</li>
							<li>Transparent operations</li>
						</ul>
					</div>
					<div class="cons">
						<h4>Cons</h4>
						<ul>
							<li>Smaller index than Google</li>
							<li>Better for EU content than US</li>
							<li>Relies partly on Bing</li>
							<li>Less comprehensive for niche queries</li>
							<li>Interface less polished than Google</li>
						</ul>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section id="setup">
				<h2>How to Use Qwant</h2>

				<div class="browser-section">
					<h3>Set as Default Search Engine</h3>
					<p>Add Qwant as your default search engine using this URL:</p>
					<code class="code-block">https://www.qwant.com/?q=%s</code>

					<h3>Browser Instructions</h3>
					<ul>
						<li><strong>Chrome:</strong> Settings → Search engine → Manage → Add (use URL above)</li>
						<li><strong>Firefox:</strong> Visit qwant.com, click address bar, add search engine</li>
						<li><strong>Safari:</strong> Not available as custom engine (use as homepage)</li>
						<li><strong>Edge:</strong> Settings → Privacy → Address bar → Manage → Add</li>
					</ul>

					<a href="/guides/set-default-search-engine" class="cta-button secondary">Full Setup Guide</a>
				</div>

				<div class="browser-section" style="margin-top: 1rem;">
					<h3>Qwant Browser Extension</h3>
					<p>Qwant offers browser extensions that:</p>
					<ul>
						<li>Set Qwant as your default search</li>
						<li>Add tracking protection</li>
						<li>Available for Chrome and Firefox</li>
					</ul>
				</div>

				<div class="browser-section" style="margin-top: 1rem;">
					<h3>Qwant Mobile Apps</h3>
					<p>Qwant has mobile apps for iOS and Android that include:</p>
					<ul>
						<li>Private search</li>
						<li>Built-in browser</li>
						<li>Tracking protection</li>
					</ul>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section id="faq">
				<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

				<div class="faq-item">
					<h3>What is Qwant search engine?</h3>
					<p>Qwant is a French privacy-focused search engine that doesn't track users or create profiles. It uses its own search index combined with Bing and complies with GDPR regulations.</p>
				</div>

				<div class="faq-item">
					<h3>Is Qwant better than Google for privacy?</h3>
					<p>Yes. Unlike Google, Qwant doesn't track searches, create user profiles, or serve personalized ads. It's based in France (EU jurisdiction) and must comply with strict GDPR privacy laws.</p>
				</div>

				<div class="faq-item">
					<h3>What is Qwant Junior?</h3>
					<p>Qwant Junior is a kid-safe search engine for children aged 6-12. It filters violent and adult content while maintaining full privacy protections. It's used in French schools and has no ads targeted at children.</p>
				</div>

				<div class="faq-item">
					<h3>Does Qwant have AI features?</h3>
					<p>Qwant has an optional AI assistant that only appears when you specifically request it. By default, you get traditional search results without any AI summaries or generated content.</p>
				</div>

				<div class="faq-item">
					<h3>Is Qwant as good as Google?</h3>
					<p>Qwant's search quality is good for most queries, especially European content. It's not as comprehensive as Google for niche or US-specific searches, but for everyday use it works well while protecting your privacy.</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<div class="next-steps">
				<h2>Next Steps</h2>
				<div class="next-links">
					<a href="/guides/best-private-search-engines">
						<span>Compare</span>
						<strong>Best Private Search Engines</strong>
					</a>
					<a href="/guides/set-default-search-engine">
						<span>Setup</span>
						<strong>Set as Default Search</strong>
					</a>
					<a href="/guides/startpage-search-engine">
						<span>Alternative</span>
						<strong>Startpage Search</strong>
					</a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</body>
</html>

